<section class="ihero"><div class="ihero-text"><div class="ihero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/appraisal-tools/">Tools</a><span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Claim Timeline Planner</span></nav><p class="kicker">Free planner</p><h1>Insurance Claim Deadline Calculator and Timeline</h1><p class="lede">Deadlines are easy to miss when you are dealing with damage. Enter your date of loss, adjust each window to your policy, and download the dates to your calendar.</p></div></div><figure class="ihero-photo"><img src="/assets/img/photos/clipboard-notes.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/clipboard-notes-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/clipboard-notes.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:900px) 100vw, 55vw" width="1200" height="800" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure></section>
<section class="sec tool-sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="rv-off">
<div class="calc" data-tool="dates">
  <div class="calc-bar"><span>Alaska claim timeline planner</span><em>Exports to your calendar</em></div>
  <div class="calc-grid">
    <div class="calc-in">
      <div><label for="t-d">Date of loss</label><input id="t-d" type="date" name="dol"></div>
      <p class="hint">Change each window to match your policy. Defaults are common figures, not legal advice.</p>
      <div class="days">
        <div><label for="t-n">Report the claim within (days)</label><input id="t-n" name="notice" inputmode="numeric" value="3"></div>
        <div><label for="t-m">Protect the property within (days)</label><input id="t-m" name="mitig" inputmode="numeric" value="7"><span class="hint">Tarps, heat, snow removal, drying.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-p">Proof of loss (days)</label><input id="t-p" name="pol" inputmode="numeric" value="60"><span class="hint">Often counted from the carrier's request.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-r">Depreciation recovery (days)</label><input id="t-r" name="rcd" inputmode="numeric" value="365"><span class="hint">Remote and winter repairs can take longer.</span></div>
        <div><label for="t-s">Suit limitation (days)</label><input id="t-s" name="suit" inputmode="numeric" value="730"><span class="hint">Use the period stated in your policy.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="calc-out" aria-live="polite">
      <ol class="timeline" data-o="timeline"></ol>
      <div class="btn-row"><button type="button" class="btn small" data-ics>Download .ics calendar file</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div></div><p class="hint center">For planning only. Results depend on what you enter and on your policy, and are not a quote, an appraisal or legal advice.</p><noscript><p class="note">This calculator needs JavaScript. You can still call us at (844) 537-1427 and we’ll run the numbers with you.</p></noscript></div></section>
<div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>The deadlines that matter</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Notice.</strong> Policies require prompt notice of loss. Report as soon as you reasonably can.</li>
<li><strong>Protecting the property.</strong> You are generally expected to take reasonable steps to prevent further damage, such as tarping, keeping heat on or removing snow.</li>
<li><strong>Proof of loss.</strong> If the carrier requests a sworn proof of loss, the policy sets a time to provide it.</li>
<li><strong>Depreciation recovery.</strong> Policies often set a window to complete repairs and claim the holdback.</li>
<li><strong>Suit limitation.</strong> Policies usually limit how long you have to sue. Talk to an Alaska attorney well before that date.</li></ul>
<h2>Using the calendar file</h2>
<p>The .ics file works with Google Calendar, Apple Calendar and Outlook. It is created in your browser and never sent to us.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Not legal advice</b>Your policy and Alaska law control the actual deadlines. If a date is close, consult an attorney promptly.</div>
<h2>Questions about this tool</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Are these default deadlines correct for my policy?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>They are placeholders. Replace each one with the period in your policy.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is my data saved?</summary><div class="faq-a"><p>No. Everything runs in your browser and nothing is stored or sent.</p></div></details></div><h2>More free tools</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-tools/appraisal-gap-fee-estimator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Appraisal Gap &amp; Fee Estimator</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-tools/depreciation-holdback-worksheet/"><small>Worksheet</small><span>RCV/ACV Depreciation Worksheet</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/appraisal-tools/roof-area-pitch-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Roof Area &amp; Pitch Calculator</span><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-stick"><div class="side-box call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through</h2><p>Free first conversation. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427">+1 (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn gold block" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri 8am–6pm Alaska Time</small></div><div class="side-b